-- title:
--   Galois representation attached to a point of the Taylor–Wiles Hecke ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, and $p$ a prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ trivial on the fixer of some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, absolutely irreducible in the sense that its base change to the algebraic closure of the residue field has no invariant subspace other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N$, let $r$ be a prime with $r \nmid N$ and $p \nmid r-1$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$, $q \mid N$ prime, $q \notin S$) such that for each prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, each valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$ and each $\sigma$ in the decomposition group acting as $x \mapsto x^\ell$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes, none in $S$ and none equal to $r$, with homomorphisms $\pi_i \colon (\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times \to \mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ (written multiplicatively), scalars $\alpha_i$ in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and characters $\mathrm{cyc}_i \colon \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q) \to (\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times$ satisfying $\sigma\mu = \mu^{\mathrm{cyc}_i(\sigma)}$ for all $\mu$ with $\mu^{q_i}=1$. Put $L = N(\prod_i q_i)r$, let $H_R \le (\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$ and $H_Q = H_R \cap \ker(\pi_i)_i$; assume the Hecke generators of the associated cohomology module pairwise commute (`OpComm`) and commute with all diamond operators $\langle u \rangle$ (`DiaComm`). Let $\mathcal O'$ be a second complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, a local $\mathcal O$-algebra, and let $\lambda$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism to $\mathcal O'$ from the Hecke ring, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}$ of the localised cohomology module $M$ generated by the Hecke and diamond operators. Then there is a complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal O''$ of characteristic zero with finite residue field which is a module-finite local $\mathcal O'$-algebra with injective structure map, a ring homomorphism $\psi$ from $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O''$, and a Galois representation $\rho$ on a free $\mathcal O''$-module of rank $2$, continuous in the sense that modulo each power of $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O''}$ it is trivial on the fixer of a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, such that: $\psi$ is compatible with the residue maps along $\mathcal O \to \mathcal O' \to \mathcal O''$; for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$ and $\ell \ne p$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring over $\ell$, $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\sigma)$ is the image of $\lambda(T_\ell)$; for every $n$, every $\sigma$ acting as $\mu \mapsto \mu^a$ on the $p^n$-th roots of unity and every $u \in H_R$ with $\pi_i(u \bmod q_i) = \pi_i(\mathrm{cyc}_i(\sigma))$ for all $i$, one has $\det \rho(\sigma) \equiv a \cdot \lambda(\langle u \rangle) \bmod p^n$; the residual representation of $\rho$ is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along $\psi$; and $\rho$ is unramified at every prime $\ell \nmid L$ with $\ell \ne p$, in the sense that $\rho$ is trivial on the inertia subgroups at $\ell$.
--
--   This is the pointwise form, with coefficients in a discrete valuation ring, of the Galois representation attached to the Hecke ring at Taylor–Wiles level: to each algebra homomorphism $\lambda$ of that Hecke ring into a discrete valuation ring it attaches a two-dimensional lift of $\bar\rho$ whose Frobenius traces are the $\lambda(T_\ell)$ and whose determinant is given by the diamond operators and the cyclotomic character. It is the input to [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_galoisRepAdic_trace_frobenius_eq_T`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_galoisRepAdic_trace_frobenius_eq_T), where the individual representations are glued into a representation over the Hecke ring itself.
